{"slug":"hp-sicilian-pin-dzp2it","studyId":"yt-QFggixdt3JQ","title":"Punishing the Sicilian Pin Variation","category":"openings","openingFamilies":["Sicilian Defense"],"color":"white","level":"intermediate","author":"Hanging Pawns","authorUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/@HangingPawns","studyUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QFggixdt3JQ","source":{"kind":"youtube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QFggixdt3JQ","channel":"Hanging Pawns","channelUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/@HangingPawns","title":"Sicilian Pin Variation (and why it's bad for black)"},"description":"An interactive course built from Stjepan Tomić's video. Learn the one move that punishes 5...Bb4, and what to do against every Black reply.","permissionNote":"Private demo built from this video to show its creator. Not published.","chapters":[{"id":"chapter-1","name":"The Pin Variation and the move that punishes it"},{"id":"chapter-2","name":"The ...Ne4 blunder"},{"id":"chapter-3","name":"The best defence: 7...Kf8"},{"id":"chapter-4","name":"Castling walks into Bh6"}],"chapterData":[{"id":"chapter-1","name":"The Pin Variation and the move that punishes it","url":"","annotator":null,"orientation":"white","startFen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 2 5","gamebook":false,"moves":[{"id":"n0","san":"Bb4","uci":"f8b4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/1b1NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 3 6","children":[{"id":"n1","san":"e5","uci":"e4e5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/4P3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 6","children":[{"id":"n2","san":"Nd5","uci":"f6d5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 7","children":[{"id":"n3","san":"Qg4","uci":"d1g4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 2 7","children":[],"comment":"Same idea as against ...Ne4: ignore the pin. c3 isn't really hanging, because White takes on g7 first. The difference is that the d5-knight isn't attacked, so Black doesn't have to move it. Better for Black than ...Ne4, but still bad.","shapes":[{"orig":"g4","dest":"g7","brush":"green"}],"nags":[1],"ts":566},{"id":"n4","san":"Bd2","uci":"c1d2","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N4/2N5/PPPB1PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq - 2 7","children":[],"comment":"Many players have chosen this passive Bd2, and Stjepan doesn't recommend it. Black takes on c3 and after ...Nxc3 bxc3 Bf8 White is better, with doubled pawns, but it's nothing major. There's a stronger move.","ts":526}],"comment":"Since ...Ne4 loses (next chapter), the knight must go to d5. Now, how does White keep the pressure on?","shapes":[{"orig":"f6","dest":"d5","brush":"green"}],"ts":513}],"comment":"The refutation. It works because of a tactical trick: you'd think it doesn't matter whether the knight goes to d5 or e4, but ...Ne4 actually loses.","nags":[1],"ts":463},{"id":"n5","san":"Nb5","uci":"d4b5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/1N6/1b2P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 4 6","children":[],"comment":"Nb5 holds the pawn with a concrete idea: after ...Ne4 Qg4 the queen hits the knight and g7. So Black shouldn't take, and equalizes with ...d5 instead. Stjepan calls it just as cheap a trick as ...Bb4: answering a suboptimal idea with a suboptimal idea.","ts":283},{"id":"n6","san":"Bd3","uci":"f1d3","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/1b1NP3/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 4 6","children":[],"comment":"Don't do this. It makes sense and White isn't worse, but it's very passive. Black plays ...d6, gets a Scheveningen structure and has perfect equality. You're not playing for an advantage.","nags":[6],"ts":415}],"comment":"This is the Pin Variation. It's the same idea as the bishop pin in the Spanish: pin the knight so it no longer defends the pawn, here on e4. If White does nothing, Black takes it. Only one move gives White an edge, but it's a tremendous one, and it's why Stjepan says Black shouldn't play this. Find it.","shapes":[{"orig":"b4","dest":"c3","brush":"red"},{"orig":"f6","dest":"e4","brush":"red"}],"ts":240}],"intro":"After 4.Nxd4 Black has a lot of options, and today's is 4...Nf6: a simple move that puts pressure on e4. 5.Nc3 is the main move for a reason. After 5.f3 d5 Black just breaks open the structure and it's very equal. Stjepan's verdict on what comes next: it's not a good opening for Black, but White still has to know it.","introTs":166,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c5","uci":"c7c5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2"},{"san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/3PP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"cxd4","uci":"c5d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3pP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nxd4","uci":"f3d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 5"},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 2 5"}]},{"id":"chapter-2","name":"The ...Ne4 blunder","url":"","annotator":null,"orientation":"white","startFen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/4P3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 6","gamebook":false,"moves":[{"id":"n0","san":"Ne4","uci":"f6e4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/4P3/1b1Nn3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 7","children":[{"id":"n1","san":"Qg4","uci":"d1g4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/4P3/1b1Nn1Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 2 7","children":[{"id":"n2","san":"Nxc3","uci":"e4c3","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/4P3/1b1N2Q1/2n5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R w KQkq - 0 8","children":[{"id":"n3","san":"Qxg7","uci":"g4g7","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1pQp/4p3/4P3/1b1N4/2n5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 0 8","children":[{"id":"n4","san":"Ne4+","uci":"c3e4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1pQp/4p3/4P3/1b1Nn3/8/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R w KQkq - 1 9","children":[{"id":"n5","san":"c3","uci":"c2c3","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1pQp/4p3/4P3/1b1Nn3/2P5/PP3PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 0 9","children":[],"comment":"The knight moved away with a discovered check, so c3: now the bishop is hanging and the rook is hanging. That's why ...Ne4 can't be played.","shapes":[{"orig":"c3","dest":"b4","brush":"green"},{"orig":"g7","dest":"h8","brush":"green"}],"nags":[1],"ts":508}],"nags":[2]}],"comment":"Even though c3 is hanging twice, that doesn't matter. Take on g7.","nags":[1],"ts":499}]}],"comment":"A very simple win: the queen attacks the pawn on g7 (and the knight).","shapes":[{"orig":"g4","dest":"g7","brush":"green"},{"orig":"g4","dest":"e4","brush":"green"}],"nags":[1],"ts":491}],"nags":[2]}],"intro":"Back to 6.e5. Normally you'd think it doesn't matter whether Black jumps into e4 with the knight or goes to d5. Here ...Ne4 actually loses, and that's why e5 is such a good move.","introTs":474,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c5","uci":"c7c5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2"},{"san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/3PP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"cxd4","uci":"c5d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3pP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nxd4","uci":"f3d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 5"},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 2 5"},{"san":"Bb4","uci":"f8b4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/1b1NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 3 6"},{"san":"e5","uci":"e4e5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/4P3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 6"}]},{"id":"chapter-3","name":"The best defence: 7...Kf8","url":"","annotator":null,"orientation":"white","startFen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 2 7","gamebook":false,"moves":[{"id":"n0","san":"Kf8","uci":"e8f8","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R w KQ - 3 8","children":[{"id":"n1","san":"Bd2","uci":"c1d2","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPPB1PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 4 8","children":[{"id":"n2","san":"h5","uci":"h7h5","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1pp1/4p3/3nP2p/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPPB1PPP/R3KB1R w KQ - 0 9","children":[{"id":"n3","san":"Qe4","uci":"g4e4","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1pp1/4p3/3nP2p/1b1NQ3/2N5/PPPB1PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 1 9","children":[],"comment":"The queen moves to e4, and after ...Bxc3 bxc3 White is supposed to have a slight edge. Even when Black knows ...Kf8 is the best move, White holds a steady edge, so Stjepan sees no reason to go for this as Black.","ts":656},{"id":"n4","san":"Qf3","uci":"g4f3","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1pp1/4p3/3nP2p/1b1N4/2N2Q2/PPPB1PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 1 9","children":[],"comment":"Also fine. Stjepan puts the queen on e4."},{"id":"n5","san":"Qg3","uci":"g4g3","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1pp1/4p3/3nP2p/1b1N4/2N3Q1/PPPB1PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 1 9","children":[],"comment":"Also fine. Stjepan puts the queen on e4."},{"id":"n6","san":"Qe2","uci":"g4e2","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1pp1/4p3/3nP2p/1b1N4/2N5/PPPBQPPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 1 9","children":[],"comment":"Also fine. Stjepan puts the queen on e4."}]}],"comment":"Unpinning. Most people find the best move here, which is ...h5. If Black doesn't play it, Black is much, much worse.","nags":[1],"ts":635},{"id":"n7","san":"a3","uci":"a2a3","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/P1N5/1PP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQ - 0 8","children":[],"comment":"Also good by the engine. Stjepan just unpins with Bd2."},{"id":"n8","san":"Bd3","uci":"f1d3","fen":"rnbq1k1r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2NB4/PPP2PPP/R1B1K2R b KQ - 4 8","children":[],"comment":"Also good by the engine. Stjepan just unpins with Bd2."}],"comment":"The best move. Black keeps g7 covered, but the bishop still pins the c3-knight.","ts":635}],"intro":"After 7.Qg4 people have tried many moves. The two main ones are castling and ...Kf8, because g7 hangs and Black has to sort that out. ...g6 is not good: after ...g6 Nb5 White is already doing well.","introTs":594,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c5","uci":"c7c5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2"},{"san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/3PP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"cxd4","uci":"c5d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3pP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nxd4","uci":"f3d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 5"},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 2 5"},{"san":"Bb4","uci":"f8b4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/1b1NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 3 6"},{"san":"e5","uci":"e4e5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/4P3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 6"},{"san":"Nd5","uci":"f6d5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 7"},{"san":"Qg4","uci":"d1g4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 2 7"}]},{"id":"chapter-4","name":"Castling walks into Bh6","url":"","annotator":null,"orientation":"white","startFen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 2 7","gamebook":false,"moves":[{"id":"n0","san":"O-O","uci":"e8g8","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R w KQ - 3 8","children":[{"id":"n1","san":"Bh6","uci":"c1h6","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1p1ppp/4p2B/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 4 8","children":[{"id":"n2","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R3KB1R w KQ - 0 9","children":[{"id":"n3","san":"Ne2","uci":"d4e2","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b4Q1/2N5/PPP1NPPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 1 9","children":[{"id":"n4","san":"Re8","uci":"f8e8","fen":"rnbqr1k1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b4Q1/2N5/PPP1NPPP/R3KB1R w KQ - 2 10","children":[{"id":"n5","san":"h4","uci":"h2h4","fen":"rnbqr1k1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b4QP/2N5/PPP1NPP1/R3KB1R b KQ - 0 10","children":[],"comment":"Black saved the rook, so just h4, and it's a total collapse. Once ...g6 is on the board, it's a hook White can undermine.","shapes":[{"orig":"h4","dest":"h5","brush":"green"}],"nags":[1],"ts":721},{"id":"n6","san":"O-O-O","uci":"e1c1","fen":"rnbqr1k1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b4Q1/2N5/PPP1NPPP/2KR1B1R b - - 3 10","children":[],"comment":"Also very strong. Stjepan castles long when Black leaves the rook, but once it has moved he goes straight for h4."},{"id":"n7","san":"Qg3","uci":"g4g3","fen":"rnbqr1k1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b6/2N3Q1/PPP1NPPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 3 10","children":[],"comment":"Also good. Once the rook has moved, Stjepan goes straight for h4."}]}],"comment":"Don't take the rook. Simply make sure c3 is defended.","nags":[1],"ts":700},{"id":"n8","san":"Nb5","uci":"d4b5","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/1N1nP3/1b4Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 1 9","children":[],"comment":"Also strong by the engine. Stjepan's move is Nde2, making sure c3 is defended."},{"id":"n9","san":"Qg3","uci":"g4g3","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b1N4/2N3Q1/PPP2PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 1 9","children":[],"comment":"Also good by the engine. Stjepan's move is Nde2, making sure c3 is defended."},{"id":"n10","san":"a3","uci":"a2a3","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1p1p1p/4p1pB/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/P1N5/1PP2PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 0 9","children":[],"comment":"Also good by the engine. Stjepan's move is Nde2, making sure c3 is defended."},{"id":"n11","san":"Bxf8","uci":"h6f8","fen":"rnbq1Bk1/pp1p1p1p/4p1p1/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R3KB1R b KQ - 0 9","children":[],"comment":"Taking this rook would actually be a mistake. Make sure c3 is defended first.","nags":[6],"ts":694}]}],"comment":"Bh6, of course. Black has to play ...g6.","shapes":[{"orig":"h6","dest":"g7","brush":"green"}],"nags":[1],"ts":684}]}],"intro":"That was ...Kf8. But the most common move is still castling, and it's a total disaster: White is winning.","introTs":677,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c5","uci":"c7c5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2"},{"san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/3PP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"cxd4","uci":"c5d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3pP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nxd4","uci":"f3d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 5"},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 2 5"},{"san":"Bb4","uci":"f8b4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/8/1b1NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 3 6"},{"san":"e5","uci":"e4e5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4pn2/4P3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 6"},{"san":"Nd5","uci":"f6d5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N4/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 7"},{"san":"Qg4","uci":"d1g4","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp1p1ppp/4p3/3nP3/1b1N2Q1/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 2 7"}]}]}